---
title: Teriyaki Chicken
image: https://www.cookingclassy.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/04/teriyaki-chicken-15.jpg
nutrition:
  calories: 258 kcal
  fat: 7 g
  saturated fat: 1 g
  carbohydrates: 15 g
  sugar: 13 g
  protein: 30 g
  sodium: 698 mg
  serving size: 1 serving
course: Main Course
time required: 15 minutes
cuisine: Japanese
tags: Teriayki Chicken
source: https://www.cookingclassy.com/teriyaki-chicken/#jump-to-recipe
servings: 4
cook time: 10 minutes
prep time: 10 minutes
---

Heat @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a #12-inch non-stick skillet{} over medium-high heat.

Add in @chicken breasts{1 1/4%lbs}(diced into 1-inch cubes) and let brown on bottom about ~{3-4%minutes} then flip and continue to cook until center registers about 160 degrees, about ~{3%minutes} longer.

While chicken is cooking, in a small mixing bowl whisk together @soy sauce{1/4%cup}, @mirin{2%tbsp}, @water{2%tbsp}, @honey{2%tbsp}, @brown sugar{1 1/2%tbsp}(packed light), @rice vinegar{1%tbsp}, @toasted sesame oil{1/4%tsp}, @ginger{2%tsp}(peeled and minced), @garlic{2%cloves}(peeled and minced) and @cornstarch{2%tsp}.

Stir the sauce in with the cooked chicken and continue to cook and toss until sauce has thickened, about ~{30-60%seconds} longer.

Serve warm garnished with @?sesame seeds{} and @?green onions{}(chopped) if desired.